extends /template/newsentry.pug

block newsvariables
  - var newskey = '2023-03-08-papers-accepted-for-icbc-and-cryptoex-2023';

//-
  block date
    | [date]

  block title
    | [title]

block newscontent
  p.card-text
  p One paper was accepted for publication at the IEEE International Conference on Blockchain and Cryptocurrency (ICBC '23).
  ul
    li "Real Estate Tokenization in Germany: Market Analysis and Concept of a Regulatory and Technical Solution" by Robert Henker, Daniel Atzberger, Willy Scheibel, and Jürgen Döllner
  p Further, three paper were accepted for publication at the IEEE Workshop on Cryptocurrency Exchanges (CryptoEx '23) which is held in conjunction with ICBC '23.
  ul
    li "Hephaistos: A Management System for Massive Order Book Data from Multiple Centralized Crypto Exchanges with an Internal Unified Order Book" by Robert Henker, Daniel Atzberger, Jan Ole Vollmer, Willy Scheibel, Jürgen Döllner, and Markus Bick
    li "OrderBookVis: A Visualization Approach for Comparing Order Books from Centralized Crypto Exchanges" by Adrian Jobst, Daniel Atzberger, Robert Henker, Willy Scheibel, and Jürgen Döllner
    li "Examining Liquidity of Exchanges and Assets and the Impact of External Events in Centralized Crypto Markets: A 2022 Study" by Adrian Jobst, Daniel Atzberger, Robert Henker, Jan Ole Vollmer, Willy Scheibel, and Jürgen Döllner
  p
    | The ICBC and CryptoEx will take place in Dubai, UAE, from May 1st to 5th. For more info, visit 
    a(href="https://icbc2023.ieee-icbc.org/" target="_blank") https://icbc2023.ieee-icbc.org/
    | .
